From e60e7376ee392acbe6d5313edf8bef2ec71e01f2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 11:25:38 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(outcomes): turn-end refresh keeps a declared wait through
 its own turn, not a newer one [daveey]

A turn-end refresh that sees the turn's own not-yet-released lease/routing token painted the chat
running and dropped the stored declaration, so the next refresh judged the reply alone and
painted done what the agent declared waiting (local-9c06dfbb, 2026-11-11).

- A running outcome carries the stored declaration.
- The concluding turn captures its own live-turn evidence (TUI marker pid+start, turn-lease
  holder+acquisition, gateway routing token+start) BEFORE scheduling its turn_end refresh
  (`capture_turn_identity`) and passes it as `refresh_outcome(concluding_turn=...)`. Only that
  evidence is discounted; any other live turn derives running. No blanket ignore_live_turn
  remains on the turn-end paths (gateway thread, TUI turn end, refused-turn auto-continue timer),
  so a late refresh can no longer overwrite a turn that started after the concluding one
  (PR1131 review t_01a1ce099f1c7723: stored `unresolved/interrupted` over a running turn).
- Rebased onto main's three-value `_live_work`; local-id classification is already fixed on main
  (kanban_session_provenance, PR1032).

Tests: tests/hermes_state/test_outcome_late_turn_end_refresh.py (late gateway refresh x routing/lease/marker,
own-turn discount, failed capture, TUI refused-turn timer with a newer turn, identity capture).
